WEBVTT

00:36.136 --> 00:38.600
[15 years ago]

00:39.976 --> 00:41.935
[Episode 3]

00:49.832 --> 00:51.629
Hey!

00:51.629 --> 00:53.736
Fighting!

01:07.520 --> 01:09.346
Alright, stop it!

01:11.399 --> 01:13.526
Hey, Chow Yun Fat!

01:13.526 --> 01:15.861
You're not even part of the Hwasan faction!

01:15.861 --> 01:17.488
So why are you jumping into

01:17.488 --> 01:21.450
other people's fights
like you've got a death wish?

01:21.450 --> 01:23.244
If you've got any sense, just go your way.

01:23.244 --> 01:25.413
You guys should go

01:25.413 --> 01:28.124
while I'm still speaking nicely.

01:28.124 --> 01:29.792
Huh?

01:29.792 --> 01:33.629
What, do you really think
you're Chow Yun Fat or something?

01:33.629 --> 01:35.339
What are you doing?

01:35.339 --> 01:37.332
Let's wrap this up.

01:48.519 --> 01:50.220
Yes, boss.

01:53.482 --> 01:56.143
Looks like there's about a dozen people.

01:58.696 --> 02:00.781
Don't worry, boss.

02:00.781 --> 02:03.108
An hour? What are you talking about?

02:03.743 --> 02:05.953
Thirty minutes.

02:05.953 --> 02:08.655
I'll wrap this up
within thirty minutes and go.

02:09.498 --> 02:11.950
What's this now?

02:17.757 --> 02:19.550
Hey!

02:19.550 --> 02:21.352
Are you a fan of Yun Fat too?

02:21.352 --> 02:23.262
Oh, yes.

02:23.262 --> 02:25.139
What's your name?

02:25.139 --> 02:27.049
I'm Ma Gong Bok!

02:28.517 --> 02:30.394
Ma Gong Bok...

02:30.394 --> 02:31.729
Nice name.

02:31.729 --> 02:33.981
You like raw fish, right?

02:33.981 --> 02:35.682
Yes!

02:44.492 --> 02:46.494
Let's wrap this up quickly
and get out of here.

02:46.494 --> 02:48.954
I'll buy you as much raw fish as you want.

02:48.954 --> 02:50.056
Okay!

03:14.600 --> 03:16.296
Jeez!

03:45.594 --> 03:46.762
Boss!

03:46.762 --> 03:49.512
Let's wrap this up quickly and go.

04:01.736 --> 04:03.176
Get over here!

04:04.264 --> 04:05.416
Nice!

04:12.163 --> 04:14.568
What are you doing? Go stop him!

04:16.680 --> 04:18.408
Darn it.

04:23.656 --> 04:25.259
You...

04:25.259 --> 04:27.043
It's been a while...

04:32.975 --> 04:34.344
Ah, boss, boss, boss!

04:34.344 --> 04:35.848
Boss, boss!

04:42.504 --> 04:43.944
Darn it.

04:48.072 --> 04:49.658
Oh my.

04:49.658 --> 04:50.659
Beom Ryong,

04:50.659 --> 04:52.328
your fist is still something else!

04:56.916 --> 04:59.251
But you seem a bit tired.

04:59.251 --> 05:01.587
I'm getting a bit sleepy.

05:01.587 --> 05:04.131
You can't get tired already!

05:04.131 --> 05:06.750
We've got to go for round two!

05:21.448 --> 05:23.048
Stay put.

05:23.048 --> 05:26.024
What the...

05:26.024 --> 05:27.560
Just finish them off!

05:36.744 --> 05:40.392
[O Ran Chinese Restaurant]

06:22.459 --> 06:25.713
Who are those guys fighting?

06:25.713 --> 06:27.715
Huh? That guy...

06:27.715 --> 06:29.925
He's our regular, the Oldboy guy.

06:29.925 --> 06:32.232
What is he doing here?

06:32.232 --> 06:33.576
Darn it.

06:35.890 --> 06:37.975
The young one's the bike owner...

06:37.975 --> 06:39.926
And the other one...

06:40.811 --> 06:42.721
That guy is Bulgae!

06:53.256 --> 06:54.856
Darn you!

06:54.856 --> 06:56.136
Darn it!

07:05.787 --> 07:08.272
Darn it!

07:27.560 --> 07:29.489
Darn it.

07:44.708 --> 07:45.896
Step on him!

07:50.839 --> 07:52.540
No!

07:52.540 --> 07:53.676
Darn it.

07:53.676 --> 07:55.464
Stop!

07:56.553 --> 07:59.422
Stop it!

08:11.592 --> 08:13.112
I was wrong...

08:13.112 --> 08:15.948
Oh dear, Gong Bok, you vicious little punk.

08:15.948 --> 08:18.951
Your boss is getting beaten,
so you finally admit it?

08:18.951 --> 08:19.994
Alright, start talking.

08:19.994 --> 08:23.205
What scheme were you
cooking up with this stunt?

08:23.205 --> 08:24.540
Did Chairman Hwang Hwa San order this?

08:24.540 --> 08:27.793
I swear I really don't know who they are!

08:27.793 --> 08:28.877
Boss In Goo!

08:28.877 --> 08:30.879
Can't you see it?

08:30.879 --> 08:33.841
- Beom Ryong has completely lost it!
- Ma Gong Bok.

08:33.841 --> 08:36.093
He's turned his life around,
focusing on the convenience store,

08:36.093 --> 08:38.887
and hasn't picked a fight
with any local thugs.

08:38.887 --> 08:41.682
How could a convenience store owner
like Kang Beom Ryong

08:41.682 --> 08:46.353
ever take you on, the big boss, In Goo?

08:46.353 --> 08:47.980
For the sake of our old times,

08:47.980 --> 08:50.024
please let it slide just this once.

08:50.024 --> 08:52.976
What a shameless punk.

08:53.777 --> 08:56.864
Old times' sake? I could tear you apart,
and it still wouldn't be enough.

08:56.864 --> 08:58.991
You little punk, I've had it with you.

08:58.991 --> 09:00.117
No!

09:00.117 --> 09:02.327
Yoo In Goo, no!

09:02.327 --> 09:05.372
You can run a convenience store
with just one hand for scanning barcodes.

09:05.372 --> 09:06.832
No, no, both hands...

09:06.832 --> 09:08.584
- Grab him.
- No! I need both arms!

09:08.584 --> 09:10.419
Both hands are needed!

09:10.419 --> 09:12.880
In Goo, no...

09:12.880 --> 09:14.339
Boss In Goo! Sir!

09:14.339 --> 09:15.799
I was wrong, it's all my fault!

09:15.799 --> 09:19.178
I didn't know my place and overstepped.

09:19.178 --> 09:21.430
It's all my fault. I apologize!

09:21.430 --> 09:22.931
So,

09:22.931 --> 09:26.185
please just give us one chance,
and if you do...

09:26.185 --> 09:28.553
we'll do whatever you tell us!

09:29.188 --> 09:30.930
Anything?

09:35.861 --> 09:38.188
Then bark like a dog.

09:44.286 --> 09:45.788
- Woof, woof!
- Boss!

09:45.788 --> 09:47.331
Woof, woof!

09:47.331 --> 09:48.916
Don't do it!

09:48.916 --> 09:50.959
Boss...

09:50.959 --> 09:53.253
I'll bark. I'll do it.

09:53.253 --> 09:56.414
Woof! Woof, woof!

09:56.414 --> 10:01.480
Woof! Woof, woof!

10:01.480 --> 10:04.973
Woof! Woof, woof!

10:04.973 --> 10:07.101
Stop!

10:07.101 --> 10:11.054
- Woof, woof!
- Woof, woof!

10:11.054 --> 10:16.514
Woof, woof!

10:22.216 --> 10:23.325
- Woof, woof!
- Woof, woof!

10:23.325 --> 10:25.151
Quiet!

10:28.831 --> 10:30.958
Woof, woof! Woof!

10:30.958 --> 10:33.877
It's so moving, it brings tears to my eyes.

10:33.877 --> 10:36.588
Cut him up before I soften up. Grab him!

10:36.588 --> 10:37.589
He barked!

10:37.589 --> 10:39.550
No! Don't do it!

10:39.550 --> 10:41.718
Cut the fake one!

10:41.718 --> 10:43.512
I said let go!

10:43.512 --> 10:45.556
Hold on!

10:45.556 --> 10:47.349
Yeah. Sergeant Kim, what's up?
I'm busy right now.

10:47.349 --> 10:49.518
Sir, are you at Yeongseon Food right now?

10:49.518 --> 10:52.563
We just received an anonymous report
of an assault there.

10:52.563 --> 10:54.690
If we move now,
we'll be there in ten minutes.

10:54.690 --> 10:56.775
A report? Which punk did that!

10:56.775 --> 10:58.861
Call it a day for now and wrap things up.

10:58.861 --> 11:00.821
Can't you even cover something like this?

11:00.821 --> 11:03.282
You better be worth the money!

11:03.282 --> 11:06.618
It's already been reported,
so I can't do anything about it.

11:06.618 --> 11:07.995
Just get out of there now.

11:07.995 --> 11:10.488
I'll delay dispatch as much as I can.

11:20.883 --> 11:22.759
Kang Beom Ryong.

11:22.759 --> 11:26.388
If you're just a mutt from the sticks,
stay on a leash and watch your house.

11:26.388 --> 11:30.091
Unless you want to get yourself beaten up
running around like that.

11:38.108 --> 11:40.110
But

11:40.110 --> 11:43.521
it's been a while since we last met.
Shame to just part ways like this, isn't it?

11:46.248 --> 11:49.161
Crap.

11:49.161 --> 11:51.863
Boss! Boss! Are you okay?

11:55.720 --> 11:56.776
[Yeongseon Food]

11:56.776 --> 11:59.304
[Yeongseon Food]

12:07.429 --> 12:08.847
- Boss, are you okay?
- Ugh, my back!

12:08.847 --> 12:11.758
I can't see anything. Take this off me.

12:14.920 --> 12:19.566
Ugh, no... Jeez.

12:19.566 --> 12:20.776
Why won't this come off?

12:20.776 --> 12:22.477
Are you alright?

12:34.665 --> 12:36.583
I'm giving you exactly three days.

12:36.583 --> 12:39.419
If you don't vacate the house by then,
we'll demolish it by force.

12:39.419 --> 12:41.380
Forced demolition... sir?

12:41.380 --> 12:42.881
Sir...

12:42.881 --> 12:45.050
If you want to report it, go ahead.

12:45.050 --> 12:47.928
But who do you think
will move faster? The cops or us?

12:47.928 --> 12:49.930
Try it if you want to know.

12:49.930 --> 12:52.057
- You know what I mean?
- Yes.

12:52.057 --> 12:53.058
We'll do it.

12:53.058 --> 12:54.559
Let's go.

12:54.559 --> 12:56.478
Nam Il? Nam Il!

12:56.478 --> 12:58.230
Nam Il! Nam Il!

12:58.230 --> 13:00.107
Nam Il? Nam Il!

13:00.107 --> 13:01.149
Nam Il, are you okay?

13:01.149 --> 13:02.359
Nam Il!

13:02.359 --> 13:03.443
Nam Il, are you okay?

13:03.443 --> 13:05.862
They... They...

13:05.862 --> 13:07.072
They're gone. They're gone...

13:07.072 --> 13:08.865
They left?

13:08.865 --> 13:10.650
They're gone. They're gone...

13:12.168 --> 13:14.280
They're gone.

13:15.580 --> 13:16.581
Boss,

13:16.581 --> 13:18.584
if you're still uneasy,

13:18.584 --> 13:20.585
should we bring in a few skilled guys

13:20.585 --> 13:22.713
and set things up properly?

13:22.713 --> 13:24.214
Skilled guys?

13:24.214 --> 13:27.884
Well, it looks like Kang Beom Ryong
has lost his bite anyway.

13:27.884 --> 13:31.462
We just wait for the right timing
and take him out quietly, don't you think?

13:33.853 --> 13:36.424
[Kim Bang Gon:
Boss, Chairman Do just arrived at the casino]

13:38.061 --> 13:41.523
Forget it. We should lay low for a while.

13:41.523 --> 13:43.275
Word is Chairman Do's
in the casino right now.

13:43.275 --> 13:44.526
Chairman Do?

13:44.526 --> 13:45.694
Wasn't he on a business trip to the US?

13:45.694 --> 13:49.614
I don't know. What's that sly fox up to,
sneaking in here again?

13:49.614 --> 13:51.783
We need to watch
Chairman Do's movements for a while.

13:51.783 --> 13:52.784
You get me?

13:52.784 --> 13:54.077
Got it, boss.

13:54.077 --> 13:58.614
Anyway, that punk Kang Beom Ryong
really does have insane luck.

14:22.064 --> 14:24.399
If you're tired,
just head in and get some rest.

14:24.399 --> 14:26.360
I'm fine.

14:26.360 --> 14:28.153
You must be tired too, boss.

14:28.153 --> 14:29.363
Tired?

14:29.363 --> 14:32.699
You think a few punches like that
would faze me?

14:32.699 --> 14:35.077
I just couldn't sleep last night,
so my condition was off.

14:35.077 --> 14:37.454
That's why I slipped a bit.

14:37.454 --> 14:41.491
If I hadn't stumbled,
I would've wiped out those punks.

14:45.879 --> 14:47.622
I'm sorry, boss.

14:48.507 --> 14:50.050
Why are you suddenly apologizing?
It doesn't suit you.

14:50.050 --> 14:52.761
Because I pointlessly chased
after Jeong Ho Myung,

14:52.761 --> 14:55.680
I ended up dragging Yoo In Goo
into this unexpectedly.

14:55.680 --> 14:58.141
From now on, I'll stop chasing

14:58.141 --> 15:00.227
after Jeong Ho Myung

15:00.227 --> 15:03.054
and give up my revenge.

15:03.772 --> 15:06.274
What? Why?

15:06.274 --> 15:10.696
The guy who messed up the Capital
wasn't Jeong Ho Myung after all.

15:10.696 --> 15:12.328
Ugh, jeez.

15:12.328 --> 15:14.074
I really got it wrong

15:14.074 --> 15:16.743
and ended up getting
tracked down by Yoo In Goo.

15:16.743 --> 15:19.413
Honestly, I think the best thing is

15:19.413 --> 15:21.706
just to forget the past

15:21.706 --> 15:23.750
and live on.

15:23.750 --> 15:25.460
So you're really going to
forget everything and live on?

15:25.460 --> 15:26.586
Yes.

15:26.586 --> 15:28.046
Like you said,

15:28.046 --> 15:29.714
from now on,

15:29.714 --> 15:31.383
I'll try to live

15:31.383 --> 15:33.677
an ordinary life,

15:33.677 --> 15:36.129
just as a regular clerk.

15:43.019 --> 15:44.762
Alright then,

15:45.564 --> 15:48.724
have a good time with her.

15:50.360 --> 15:52.854
Don't go! Don't go! Where are you going?

15:53.530 --> 15:55.481
G-Gong Bok...

15:58.493 --> 15:59.995
What?

15:59.995 --> 16:01.288
Did thieves break into the convenience store?

16:01.288 --> 16:03.039
What?

16:03.039 --> 16:04.458
Wait, sir!

16:04.458 --> 16:06.543
- Your face is...
- Wait, wait.

16:06.543 --> 16:08.128
Oh, this?

16:08.128 --> 16:09.912
It's nothing.

16:14.509 --> 16:16.752
Did gangsters do this to you?

16:18.847 --> 16:22.392
G-Gangsters? No, no, not at all.

16:22.392 --> 16:25.353
There've been a lot of gangsters
showing up at the casino lately.

16:25.353 --> 16:28.231
You're having trouble with them, right?
I'll deal with them!

16:28.231 --> 16:29.649
- No, no, no!
- No.

16:29.649 --> 16:30.859
- No, it's not!
- No!

16:30.859 --> 16:32.194
Oh, sorry.

16:32.194 --> 16:33.695
Not gangsters.

16:33.695 --> 16:35.906
Just drunk troublemakers did this.

16:35.906 --> 16:37.741
I already talked them down,

16:37.741 --> 16:39.984
so you don't need to report it,
absolutely not.

16:42.120 --> 16:43.121
Even so...

16:43.121 --> 16:45.999
Oh, right! You came
to buy lunchboxes, didn't you?

16:45.999 --> 16:47.992
I doubt any are still intact.

17:06.478 --> 17:10.014
If wounds are not treated properly,
they can get infected.

17:19.699 --> 17:23.194
Even if you don't report it,
you should get treatment.

17:25.497 --> 17:27.198
Treatment?

17:28.333 --> 17:29.793
Anyway,

17:29.793 --> 17:31.586
whether it's drunk people or gangsters,

17:31.586 --> 17:33.296
anyone who blindly uses force

17:33.296 --> 17:36.550
to hit others like that
should just be wiped out.

17:36.550 --> 17:37.592
So from now on,

17:37.592 --> 17:39.594
if anything like this happens,

17:39.594 --> 17:41.221
make sure you report it immediately.

17:41.221 --> 17:43.640
- Yes...
- Oh!

17:43.640 --> 17:46.509
If reporting feels burdensome,

17:47.727 --> 17:49.929
you can contact me directly.

17:51.147 --> 17:53.275
[Officer Park Mi Kyeong]
Oh, I guess even patrol officers

17:53.275 --> 17:56.194
- have business cards like this these days.
- I made them myself.

17:56.194 --> 17:57.445
Limited to just a hundred copies.

17:57.445 --> 17:59.447
Oh my, a limited edition?
That must be very precious.

17:59.447 --> 18:00.740
W-Why are you giving this to me?

18:00.740 --> 18:03.785
Citizens who work as hard
as you do are exactly

18:03.785 --> 18:05.954
the ones we police officers
are supposed to protect.

18:05.954 --> 18:07.706
So please make sure

18:07.706 --> 18:09.165
- to contact me.
- Yeah.

18:09.165 --> 18:11.209
Please contact me!

18:11.209 --> 18:12.910
Okay.

18:17.549 --> 18:19.750
Take care.

18:27.809 --> 18:29.894
I'm sorry, boss.

18:29.894 --> 18:31.855
You should live an ordinary,

18:31.855 --> 18:34.691
happy life.

18:34.691 --> 18:36.610
I'll take responsibility

18:36.610 --> 18:39.353
and finish what I started.

18:40.614 --> 18:42.324
What? Are you sure?

18:42.324 --> 18:43.825
Bulgae?

18:43.825 --> 18:45.660
I'm sure.

18:45.660 --> 18:49.205
The dress he was wearing
on that ferry ten years ago

18:49.205 --> 18:50.415
was found inside the house.

18:50.415 --> 18:52.626
And the item? Was the item there too?

18:52.626 --> 18:55.712
I searched everything.

18:55.712 --> 18:57.913
[No signal]
But the receiver isn't picking up anything.

18:58.632 --> 19:01.092
It doesn't seem to be inside the house.

19:01.092 --> 19:04.095
[No signal]
We'll probably need to approach this

19:04.095 --> 19:06.097
from a different direction, more carefully.

19:06.097 --> 19:07.307
W-Why?

19:07.307 --> 19:08.975
Why? Is there a problem?

19:08.975 --> 19:11.144
Is Bulgae some ordinary guy?

19:11.144 --> 19:12.979
From living on Yeongseondo Island

19:12.979 --> 19:15.315
[Pay slip]
for the past ten years while working,

19:15.315 --> 19:17.984
to infiltrating a household
of the grandfather and grandson.

19:17.984 --> 19:20.820
- It could be a trap.
- A trap?

19:20.820 --> 19:22.697
Bulgae wasn't

19:22.697 --> 19:25.399
the only one at Yeongseon Food.

19:26.242 --> 19:27.786
The guy with the scar on his forehead,

19:27.786 --> 19:30.163
high schooler, that country bumpkin,

19:30.163 --> 19:32.040
and...

19:32.040 --> 19:34.793
our regular, the Oldboy guy.

19:34.793 --> 19:38.088
Seeing him with Bulgae
feels awkward no matter how I think about it.

19:38.088 --> 19:39.798
It could be a coincidence.

19:39.798 --> 19:41.383
The guy who's been
hanging around me for ten years

19:41.383 --> 19:44.219
just happened to be with Bulgae
on that day, and you call that coincidence?

19:44.219 --> 19:46.554
You know too, right? Back then...

19:46.554 --> 19:49.307
There was a third person.

19:49.307 --> 19:51.559
Let's start with
what is clearly in front of us

19:51.559 --> 19:53.978
and dig into it step by step.

19:53.978 --> 19:57.816
I'll take this Oldboy guy in for questioning.

19:57.816 --> 19:59.526
Alright, Ho Myung.

19:59.526 --> 20:01.695
We're almost there. Be careful.

20:01.695 --> 20:05.490
- It's our first mission in ten years.
- Come on, why are you like this?

20:05.490 --> 20:07.525
Did you forget who I am?

20:32.104 --> 20:34.824
[September 2010]

22:06.664 --> 22:08.029
Come on...

22:08.029 --> 22:11.398
Resorting to classic tactics?

22:24.616 --> 22:26.280
[Ms. Lee]

22:27.144 --> 22:29.592
Oh, my.

22:29.592 --> 22:31.344
- Hello?
- Mr. Bong!

22:31.344 --> 22:34.264
How could you just skip work without a word?

22:34.264 --> 22:36.266
Ms. Lee.

22:36.266 --> 22:39.368
I'm really not feeling well.

22:41.062 --> 22:44.107
I told you I can't cover for you anymore.

22:44.107 --> 22:47.443
I'll crawl into work tomorrow if I have to,
just this once...

22:47.443 --> 22:49.195
If you keep skipping work,

22:49.195 --> 22:51.865
just know you'll be fired.

22:51.865 --> 22:54.149
I was just...

23:04.200 --> 23:05.896
Jeez.

23:53.480 --> 23:55.560
[Officer Park Mi Kyeong]

23:57.512 --> 24:01.256
[Officer Park Mi Kyeong]

24:18.216 --> 24:22.088
[Friendly Convenience Store]

24:52.444 --> 24:53.444
Sir!

24:53.444 --> 24:55.396
What are you doing, part-timer?

24:56.197 --> 24:58.023
Going to a wedding?

25:00.285 --> 25:02.328
Yes...

25:02.328 --> 25:04.279
I'm going far away.

25:05.790 --> 25:07.491
Sir.

25:08.418 --> 25:10.119
I've ordered

25:11.462 --> 25:14.132
a lot of Seoraksan cigarettes for you.

25:14.132 --> 25:15.591
So, in the future,

25:15.591 --> 25:17.418
please keep coming

25:18.052 --> 25:20.930
to our convenience store.

25:20.930 --> 25:22.140
Huh?

25:22.140 --> 25:23.841
What's going on?

25:52.795 --> 25:54.130
Surprise!

25:54.130 --> 25:55.214
You're early, Mr. Yoo.

25:55.214 --> 25:56.215
You came early?

25:56.215 --> 25:57.842
You call people over
first thing in the morning,

25:57.842 --> 25:59.343
and what are you eating?

25:59.343 --> 26:00.678
Still got that attitude, huh?

26:00.678 --> 26:02.096
People die when they change, you know.

26:02.096 --> 26:04.506
So what, you want to grab
brunch or something?

26:04.506 --> 26:07.060
[Chairman of Heaven Hotel & Casino,
Do Hyeon Tae]

26:07.060 --> 26:08.728
Why would I ruin my stomach over that?

26:08.728 --> 26:11.314
Just say what you have to say.

26:11.314 --> 26:12.899
Okay.

26:12.899 --> 26:14.442
Well...

26:14.442 --> 26:17.528
Alright, I'll get straight
to the point. Have a seat.

26:17.528 --> 26:19.313
Executive Director Nam.

26:20.232 --> 26:22.391
Okay.

26:27.497 --> 26:30.458
[Medical certificate]
You beat up security staff a few days ago.

26:30.458 --> 26:32.460
Come on, you can't just
beat up salaried workers

26:32.460 --> 26:34.962
covered by the four major insurances
like street thugs.

26:34.962 --> 26:36.881
You should know better.

26:36.881 --> 26:39.875
I told them to just settle this nicely.

26:40.676 --> 26:42.095
So what, you want compensation?

26:42.095 --> 26:43.096
No.

26:43.096 --> 26:44.430
No, no, no, no.

26:44.430 --> 26:48.226
I can cover the medical bills myself,
so that's fine.

26:48.226 --> 26:51.687
But I'm suddenly curious about something.

26:51.687 --> 26:53.189
Why?

26:53.189 --> 26:55.942
I don't understand. Why?

26:55.942 --> 26:58.444
Stop speaking English. Can't you
speak Korean when we're being polite?

26:58.444 --> 27:01.197
I mean, why go as far as
beating up security guys

27:01.197 --> 27:03.533
just to check the CCTV?

27:03.533 --> 27:06.110
What was on that CCTV?

27:06.994 --> 27:07.995
Like,

27:07.995 --> 27:10.414
did something happen

27:10.414 --> 27:12.208
to Heaven Capital?

27:12.208 --> 27:13.626
Don't test me.

27:13.626 --> 27:14.961
Test?

27:14.961 --> 27:18.422
Come on, why would I test you
at a time like this?

27:18.422 --> 27:21.759
Mr. Yoo, any problem with your business?

27:21.759 --> 27:23.761
- Stupid...
- You fake Yankee!

27:23.761 --> 27:25.963
Speak Korean!

27:32.395 --> 27:34.096
You're really...

27:35.912 --> 27:37.322
Darn it.

27:41.654 --> 27:43.531
Whoa, whoa, whoa, calm down.

27:43.531 --> 27:45.607
Calm down, man, Mr. Nam.

27:45.607 --> 27:47.326
Darn it.

27:47.326 --> 27:49.245
Why are you all getting so worked up?

27:49.245 --> 27:50.830
Huh? How crude.

27:50.830 --> 27:51.914
I was just asking because

27:51.914 --> 27:54.459
- I'm worried about you, Mr. Yoo.
- Worried?

27:54.459 --> 27:55.585
Yeah.

27:55.585 --> 27:56.794
Mr. Yoo,

27:56.794 --> 27:59.380
Heaven Capital is your business, but,

27:59.380 --> 28:02.592
Heaven Hotel and Casino is my business, so,

28:02.592 --> 28:04.594
we're on the same boat called Heaven.

28:04.594 --> 28:07.096
If you cause trouble for no reason
and Mr. Han hears about it,

28:07.096 --> 28:09.640
it'll be bad for both of us.

28:09.640 --> 28:12.351
We're partners on the same ship, right?

28:12.351 --> 28:14.187
When problems come up,
we should help each other, right?

28:14.187 --> 28:15.229
Help?

28:15.229 --> 28:18.649
You help me? Really?

28:18.649 --> 28:21.727
You're the kind of guy who'd wipe out
my entire business if I slip up.

28:23.654 --> 28:25.573
I'll handle this myself,

28:25.573 --> 28:27.825
so just keep your mouth shut, got it?

28:27.825 --> 28:30.411
Oh, shut up?

28:30.411 --> 28:31.662
Okay!

28:31.662 --> 28:33.247
No problem.

28:33.247 --> 28:35.041
Bye.

28:35.041 --> 28:36.825
Even when I try to help, he refuses.

28:40.840 --> 28:42.378
Alright.

28:44.717 --> 28:47.345
Mr. Yoo's drug-laced beef jerky
is circulating in the casino.

28:47.345 --> 28:49.046
Drug?

28:53.448 --> 28:54.852
Wow.

28:54.852 --> 28:56.229
Mr. Yoo is quite diligent.

28:56.229 --> 28:58.940
Getting involved unnecessarily
could cause problems.

28:58.940 --> 29:01.058
Should we report this to Mr. Han?

29:01.058 --> 29:03.419
Well...

29:07.281 --> 29:08.866
For now,

29:08.866 --> 29:11.276
let's keep this one on hold.

29:12.954 --> 29:14.830
Or instead,

29:14.830 --> 29:16.123
how about we

29:16.123 --> 29:19.585
dig into this jerky business
ourselves in detail?

29:19.585 --> 29:21.295
If this portfolio checks out,

29:21.295 --> 29:23.631
it wouldn't be a bad idea
for us to take it over.

29:23.631 --> 29:25.925
And keep following up on the Capital case.

29:25.925 --> 29:29.252
Yes, I'll look into it and report back.

29:41.148 --> 29:43.359
I told you to keep the security team's
mouths shut, didn't I?

29:43.359 --> 29:46.028
Can't you even handle that one simple thing?

29:46.028 --> 29:47.947
Might as well advertise
that we've got a problem, huh?

29:47.947 --> 29:49.615
I'm sorry, boss.

29:49.615 --> 29:51.316
Sorry? My foot.

29:57.748 --> 29:59.458
Stop following me and move your car.

29:59.458 --> 30:01.159
Understood.

30:03.816 --> 30:06.056
The number you dialed is not available now.
Please leave a message...

30:40.374 --> 30:42.710
Enough already...

30:42.710 --> 30:45.512
- Stop it.
- Take more!

31:17.328 --> 31:20.122
Where are you from, a newspaper?

31:20.122 --> 31:21.874
Or maybe a broadcasting station?

31:21.874 --> 31:23.084
Hello.

31:23.084 --> 31:24.627
I apologize for the late greeting.

31:24.627 --> 31:25.961
I'm from

31:25.961 --> 31:28.756
the Criminal Division
of the Imcheon District Prosecutors' Office,

31:28.756 --> 31:30.832
[Kang Yeong Ae, Supreme Prosecutor's Office]
Prosecutor Kang Young Ae.

31:32.426 --> 31:34.387
I have a few questions I'd like to ask.

31:34.387 --> 31:38.516
What business could a prosecutor
possibly have with an old man like me?

31:38.516 --> 31:40.893
I've been in prison for so long,

31:40.893 --> 31:43.896
so I don't really know
what's going on outside.

31:43.896 --> 31:45.439
This is about the 10-year-old murder

31:45.439 --> 31:48.025
of National Security Advisor Kwon Sun Bok,

31:48.025 --> 31:50.694
the case that put you in prison,
Mr. Hwang Hwa San.

31:50.694 --> 31:54.815
- You probably know it better than anyone.
- That case is over.

31:55.825 --> 31:57.493
Why are you asking about it?

31:57.493 --> 32:00.287
If the real killer wasn't caught,

32:00.287 --> 32:02.623
it's not a closed case yet, is it?

32:02.623 --> 32:05.793
I don't want gossip like 'personal revenge'

32:05.793 --> 32:07.586
or 'a plot by Chief Kwon Sun Bok's rival.'

32:07.586 --> 32:10.923
Not these rumors spread by tabloids.

32:10.923 --> 32:13.926
I want the truth.

32:13.926 --> 32:15.678
Mr. Hwang Hwa San,

32:15.678 --> 32:19.297
is this the person who framed you for murder

32:21.684 --> 32:23.427
and sent you to prison?

32:31.485 --> 32:34.688
I don't know what you're talking about.

32:35.615 --> 32:39.994
- Mr. Hwang.
- If you're going to believe rumors,

32:39.994 --> 32:42.320
at least pick the believable ones.

32:43.080 --> 32:46.825
Oh, dear. Are you that scared
of Han Kyung Wook?

32:55.259 --> 32:56.886
Prosecutor,

32:56.886 --> 32:59.597
I've lost the organization
I built my whole life,

32:59.597 --> 33:02.641
and now in my later years,
I'm suffering in prison.

33:02.641 --> 33:04.643
What could I possibly

33:04.643 --> 33:08.105
have left to fear now?

33:08.105 --> 33:11.609
Being used without getting
anything in return,

33:11.609 --> 33:15.896
that's what I hate.

33:16.864 --> 33:18.991
I'm not trying to use you right now.

33:18.991 --> 33:21.285
I just want a fair deal for both sides.

33:21.285 --> 33:22.661
I need to solve this case,

33:22.661 --> 33:25.822
and you should get a chance
to be released, Mr. Hwang.

33:28.250 --> 33:30.628
For it to be a fair deal,

33:30.628 --> 33:31.795
shouldn't I

33:31.795 --> 33:36.509
get out of prison first?

33:36.509 --> 33:41.055
If you bring me the real killer
who killed Chief Kwon Sun Bok,

33:41.055 --> 33:44.925
and then I'll talk.

33:48.562 --> 33:50.680
So you know who the real killer is?

33:53.317 --> 33:55.560
Who is that person?

34:00.324 --> 34:02.785
It's not

34:02.785 --> 34:05.663
a person.

34:05.663 --> 34:08.657
It's the dog

34:09.667 --> 34:12.661
I used to raise.

34:20.844 --> 34:22.930
She's just scurrying around everywhere.

34:22.930 --> 34:25.224
She's not Nongae. She's just a stray dog.

34:25.224 --> 34:27.226
Should I report it right away?

34:27.226 --> 34:28.686
Hold on.

34:28.686 --> 34:31.054
Let's check where she's heading first.

34:42.344 --> 34:44.392
[Restricted number]

34:50.624 --> 34:51.959
Hello, this is Prosecutor Kang Young Ae.

34:51.959 --> 34:53.127
Prosecutor Kang,

34:53.127 --> 34:55.963
digging around everywhere
isn't going to solve anything.

34:55.963 --> 34:59.133
You need to watch
what's behind you as you go.

34:59.133 --> 35:01.927
- Who is this?
- I can't tell you that yet.

35:01.927 --> 35:04.096
The people in the white car ahead,

35:04.096 --> 35:06.089
don't they look familiar?

35:11.729 --> 35:13.188
You see the road ahead?

35:13.188 --> 35:15.065
Go straight at the intersection.

35:15.065 --> 35:16.692
I'll handle the rest.

35:16.692 --> 35:18.560
Hold on, hello?

35:58.859 --> 36:00.694
Oh, ma'am!

36:00.694 --> 36:02.029
- Are you okay?
- Oh, I...

36:02.029 --> 36:03.447
Police! We're police!

36:03.447 --> 36:04.698
- Hey.
- Ma'am!

36:04.698 --> 36:06.784
Ma'am, are you okay? Ma'am, are you okay?

36:06.784 --> 36:08.744
- Hey! Hey!
- Ma'am!

36:08.744 --> 36:10.445
Oh, no.

36:14.375 --> 36:15.542
What? What's going on?

36:15.542 --> 36:17.002
That person is...

36:17.002 --> 36:18.253
Sir!

36:18.253 --> 36:19.996
No...

36:38.664 --> 36:40.014
Hello.

36:40.014 --> 36:41.521
It's been a while.

36:42.152 --> 36:43.478
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

36:44.906 --> 36:48.400
You've had a long journey.
I'll escort you inside.

36:57.160 --> 36:59.277
Let's see.

36:59.277 --> 37:01.111
They wrote something new.

37:01.111 --> 37:05.288
[Tokyo Ryusei-gumi, Direct Affiliate Yakuza,
VP of Toyo Finance, Nakatomo Ryuichi]

37:09.448 --> 37:11.618
[Chinese Triad Officer,
Head of Future Strategy Office]

37:11.618 --> 37:12.840
[Hunan Construction, Li Guo Feng]

37:13.448 --> 37:18.086
Nothing has even started yet.
Isn't that the case?

37:18.086 --> 37:20.313
I heard the city has been delaying the review

37:20.313 --> 37:23.144
for quite some time now, and as a result,

37:23.144 --> 37:27.016
the land approval process has been stuck
for several months without any progress.

37:27.016 --> 37:31.240
I'm starting to doubt whether
you even have the ability to handle this.

37:34.872 --> 37:38.041
It's true the project is delayed,

37:38.041 --> 37:40.210
but this situation was fully anticipated.

37:40.210 --> 37:42.755
If I win the mayoral election,

37:42.755 --> 37:45.549
the permits will be resolved immediately.

37:45.549 --> 37:49.428
After that, the project
will move full speed ahead.

37:49.428 --> 37:51.430
So please be patient

37:51.430 --> 37:53.506
and watch.

37:54.888 --> 37:56.776
Win the election?

37:56.776 --> 38:03.240
The difference in support rate
between you and your opponent is only 0.5%.

38:03.240 --> 38:06.696
Can you really say with 100% certainty
that you will win?

38:06.696 --> 38:12.715
Besides, your opponent
has already built up a strong network.

38:13.672 --> 38:16.872
The advantage is about to be
overturned, isn't it?

38:32.888 --> 38:35.140
What about Kim Seon Jung?

38:35.140 --> 38:36.975
It's tougher than expected.

38:36.975 --> 38:38.393
No matter how thoroughly
we scour his accounts,

38:38.393 --> 38:40.762
not a speck of dust comes out.

38:40.762 --> 38:42.147
[Report on Candidate Kim Seon Jung]

38:42.147 --> 38:44.191
There's nothing we can turn into a scandal?

38:44.191 --> 38:46.276
Ever since his time as a teacher
on Yeongseondo Island,

38:46.276 --> 38:48.028
[Basic information on Kim Seon Jung]
he was so well-respected,

38:48.028 --> 38:50.405
[Recent activities of Candidate Kim]
not even a single rumor about bribes.

38:50.405 --> 38:51.907
We checked his connections too,

38:51.907 --> 38:54.076
but his only family is his wife.

38:54.076 --> 38:57.162
His wife runs an orphanage
called Ja Ae-won Orphanage

38:57.162 --> 38:59.665
and also has an excellent reputation.

38:59.665 --> 39:02.951
So he's been spotless his whole life?

39:05.087 --> 39:06.755
[The recent year financial activity]
It seems Kim Seon Jung

39:06.755 --> 39:08.131
has also stepped in as a donor

39:08.131 --> 39:10.583
and is taking a special interest
in Ja Ae-won Orphanage.

39:12.719 --> 39:14.721
Should we dig into that connection more?

39:14.721 --> 39:17.048
Set up a meeting.

39:17.891 --> 39:20.644
No matter how squeaky clean he is,

39:20.644 --> 39:25.274
a few bad storms can muddy anyone.

39:25.274 --> 39:27.192
Set up a meeting and get him in
as soon as possible.

39:27.192 --> 39:28.893
Yes, sir.

39:50.674 --> 39:51.758
Hello.

39:51.758 --> 39:55.429
You are Mr. Jeong, the owner of
O Ran Chinese Restaurant, right?

39:55.429 --> 39:59.057
Nice to meet you.
But why am I tied up like this?

39:59.057 --> 40:02.051
"You are Mr. Jeong, the owner of
O Ran Chinese Restaurant, right?"

40:04.521 --> 40:09.109
I should've known when you kept ordering
nothing but those unpopular fried dumplings.

40:09.109 --> 40:10.485
Pardon?

40:10.485 --> 40:12.321
Sir, what are you talking about?

40:12.321 --> 40:17.358
Why did you hang around me for ten years,
eating only fried dumplings?

40:18.619 --> 40:22.030
What do you mean?
Because the dumplings are good.

40:23.415 --> 40:25.241
- Really?
- Yeah!

40:26.043 --> 40:28.745
Yeah, that's the way to answer.

40:29.796 --> 40:31.506
This...

40:31.506 --> 40:34.792
It's been a while since I last did this,
so I'm not sure if it'll go well.

40:35.844 --> 40:39.973
You know what this is?
It's what the CIA guys use, you know?

40:39.973 --> 40:41.642
They call it the truth serum.

40:41.642 --> 40:45.428
Once injected, you'll spill everything
you know and even what you don't.

40:46.229 --> 40:47.814
They developed it secretly

40:47.814 --> 40:51.443
because criminals kept stalling
with the right to remain silent.

40:51.443 --> 40:53.987
It works insanely well.

40:53.987 --> 40:57.273
Only downside is the side effects.

40:58.992 --> 41:00.953
If you're unlucky,

41:00.953 --> 41:05.782
there's about a 50%

41:09.294 --> 41:11.880
- You know what I mean?
- Getting dizzy?

41:11.880 --> 41:14.666
You'll be drooling all the time.

41:15.717 --> 41:17.844
No!

41:17.844 --> 41:20.013
Stay back! Don't come any closer, you punk!

41:20.013 --> 41:22.516
You punk, stop!

41:22.516 --> 41:23.684
Don't do it!

41:23.684 --> 41:25.259
Hey, hey! Don't do it!

41:26.395 --> 41:28.596
I almost died, seriously!

41:30.899 --> 41:32.359
Don't do it, don't do it!

41:32.359 --> 41:33.986
Don't do it! You're not really
going to inject me, are you?

41:33.986 --> 41:35.487
I'll ask you one last time.

41:35.487 --> 41:36.989
This is driving me crazy!

41:36.989 --> 41:38.031
Who are you really?

41:38.031 --> 41:40.858
I told you, I really went there
because the dumplings are good!

41:41.660 --> 41:43.620
The dumplings are good?

41:43.620 --> 41:46.873
The dumplings you've been eating
for ten years

41:46.873 --> 41:50.711
are factory-made frozen dumplings, you idiot.

41:50.711 --> 41:53.380
I guess I just really like frozen dumplings!

41:53.380 --> 41:55.173
This might sting a bit. Just bear with it.

41:55.173 --> 41:57.092
- Don't do it, don't do it!
- Come on, just bear with it.

41:57.092 --> 41:58.844
- Don't do it!
- Just a bit, just a bit, hold on.

41:58.844 --> 42:00.262
It's okay.

42:00.262 --> 42:02.130
Don't do it! Stop, stop!

42:02.130 --> 42:04.182
No, wait!

42:04.182 --> 42:05.183
Hwasan faction! Hwasan faction!

42:05.183 --> 42:07.728
Hwasan... ugh, it stings!
Hwasan faction! Hwasan faction!

42:07.728 --> 42:09.354
- Hwasan faction! Hwasan faction!
- Hwasan faction?

42:09.354 --> 42:11.606
The Hwasan faction of Hwang Hwa San,

42:11.606 --> 42:12.649
the one arrested for killing Chief Kwon?

42:12.649 --> 42:13.984
It was a setup!

42:13.984 --> 42:17.228
We were framed by Han Kyung Wook too!

42:19.031 --> 42:21.033
Stop beating around the bush
and talk straight.

42:21.033 --> 42:24.777
Ten years ago, when you were
on a mission on the ferry,

42:30.792 --> 42:32.627
Han Kyung Wook gave us the order

42:32.627 --> 42:34.463
to retrieve an item.

42:34.463 --> 42:36.590
So you were the one
who suddenly interfered that day?

42:36.590 --> 42:38.091
Yes!

42:38.091 --> 42:40.960
But things went wrong, seriously...

42:41.928 --> 42:46.266
That Bulgae guy or whoever
you're looking for stole the item,

42:46.266 --> 42:50.595
and we are trying to take out Han Kyung Wook
for what he did to our chairman!

42:55.192 --> 42:56.693
We're

42:56.693 --> 42:59.613
victims of Han Kyung Wook too.

42:59.613 --> 43:01.406
Do you know what happened
to our Hwasan faction

43:01.406 --> 43:03.158
after that incident ten years ago?

43:03.158 --> 43:04.859
- Be careful!
- Stop there!

43:07.208 --> 43:08.784
Darn it.

43:13.543 --> 43:14.586
Boss!

43:14.586 --> 43:16.254
Boss!

43:16.254 --> 43:18.882
That punk Han Kyung Wook teamed up

43:18.882 --> 43:20.926
with Yoo In Goo and set a perfect trap!

43:20.926 --> 43:22.761
Looks like this is the end
of the Hwasan faction too.

43:22.761 --> 43:24.930
It's not over yet!

43:24.930 --> 43:27.557
That NIS guy who interfered with us

43:27.557 --> 43:29.226
- is on Yeongseondo Island right now!
- Jeez.

43:29.226 --> 43:30.685
- Yeongseondo Island?
- Yes.

43:30.685 --> 43:33.230
I saw it with my own eyes.

43:33.230 --> 43:34.606
He went in to retrieve the thing

43:34.606 --> 43:36.441
that Bulgae guy was looking for!

43:36.441 --> 43:38.944
That thing Han Kyung Wook
is searching for desperately,

43:38.944 --> 43:41.145
if only we had that...

43:44.991 --> 43:46.409
You guys

43:46.409 --> 43:50.330
go to Yeongseondo Island
and find that item no matter what, okay?

43:50.330 --> 43:52.082
See you later.

43:52.082 --> 43:54.312
Go, go!

43:55.460 --> 43:57.295
- Catch them! Hurry!
- Boss!

43:57.295 --> 44:00.200
- Hurry up!
- Yes, got it!

44:00.200 --> 44:01.672
- We must go!
- Back then,

44:01.672 --> 44:03.343
finding that item was our only hope

44:03.343 --> 44:05.220
of clearing our boss' name

44:05.220 --> 44:08.297
and rebuilding the Hwasan faction!

44:09.808 --> 44:12.561
[O Ran Chinese Restaurant]
Right, Jeong Ho Myung.

44:12.561 --> 44:15.730
Jeong Ho Myung is NIS's top agent,

44:15.730 --> 44:17.816
so he can find it, no...

44:17.816 --> 44:19.526
He will find it for us.

44:19.526 --> 44:21.227
Thank you!

44:21.862 --> 44:23.563
Stop it!

44:25.240 --> 44:26.491
Boss.

44:26.491 --> 44:28.285
It's already been three months!

44:28.285 --> 44:31.413
How long are we going to
just watch that punk fooling around?

44:31.413 --> 44:33.165
If we rush in and mess it up again
like last time,

44:33.165 --> 44:35.241
are you going to take responsibility?

44:36.126 --> 44:37.919
That guy may not look like it,

44:37.919 --> 44:40.130
but he's NIS's top black ops agent.

44:40.130 --> 44:43.457
There's definitely a reason
he infiltrated that Chinese restaurant.

44:44.176 --> 44:48.296
We just need to strike
the moment he gets the item.

44:50.682 --> 44:53.226
Yeah, we just have to wait.

44:53.226 --> 44:54.519
That Chinese restaurant delivery guy

44:54.519 --> 44:57.314
must be acting like that
because he has some big plan.

44:57.314 --> 44:59.941
He wouldn't just sit around doing nothing.

44:59.941 --> 45:03.862
He must be acting like that
because there's something

45:03.862 --> 45:06.573
at the Chinese restaurant
that can help him find the item.

45:06.573 --> 45:09.117
Waiting endlessly
every single day for a whole year,

45:09.117 --> 45:11.119
we prayed and prayed.

45:11.119 --> 45:13.288
Praying for Jeong Ho Myung
to finally make a move.

45:13.288 --> 45:16.458
Praying to escape this hell.

45:16.458 --> 45:18.126
But you seemed

45:18.126 --> 45:21.463
too busy fooling around
with the Chinese restaurant owner's daughter

45:21.463 --> 45:23.006
to even think about finding the item.

45:23.006 --> 45:25.791
[For lease]
You looked pretty darn happy too.

45:27.427 --> 45:30.388
You think we started working
at a convenience store because we wanted to?

45:30.388 --> 45:32.641
We've got to hang in there somehow,
even if it's by doing that.

45:32.641 --> 45:34.142
This is

45:34.142 --> 45:37.608
- all your fault, Jeong Ho Myung!
- Jeez, come on!

45:44.277 --> 45:45.654
- Have you lost your mind?
- Oh, my.

45:45.654 --> 45:48.031
You're talking nonsense.

45:48.031 --> 45:50.116
Come on, despite all that,
what kind of gangsters

45:50.116 --> 45:51.656
run a convenience store for ten years?

45:51.656 --> 45:52.712
And what about you?

45:52.712 --> 45:53.954
NIS's top ace

45:53.954 --> 45:55.830
- running a Chinese restaurant?
- What?

45:55.830 --> 45:57.082
And how was I supposed to know?

45:57.082 --> 45:59.125
That I'd end up living as
a convenience store clerk for ten years.

45:59.125 --> 46:01.795
Jeong Ho Myung, weren't you NIS's ace?

46:01.795 --> 46:04.422
If you had just found the item on time,
none of this would've happened!

46:04.422 --> 46:05.590
You little punk!

46:05.590 --> 46:06.925
Are you blaming me right now?

46:06.925 --> 46:08.218
Do you think I enjoyed living like this?

46:08.218 --> 46:09.427
It looked like you did.

46:09.427 --> 46:10.887
You became the son-in-law
of that famous restaurant's owner,

46:10.887 --> 46:12.097
got married, and had a kid.

46:12.097 --> 46:13.431
You seemed pretty darn happy.

46:13.431 --> 46:16.393
Compared to me working 12-hour shifts,
that looks like paradise.

46:16.393 --> 46:18.520
Isn't that right?

46:18.520 --> 46:19.521
You little punk!

46:19.521 --> 46:20.814
You were born in '92, right?
Year of the Monkey.

46:20.814 --> 46:23.349
- Why did you kick me?
- Are you going to speak nicely?

46:24.484 --> 46:26.435
Please save me...

46:31.408 --> 46:34.193
Please... I beg you.

46:49.718 --> 46:52.595
Just thinking about how
you blew that operation ten years ago

46:52.595 --> 46:54.806
makes my blood boil.

46:54.806 --> 46:59.144
But what would change even if
I caught a useless small fry like you now?

46:59.144 --> 47:01.896
I'd rather use you as bait

47:01.896 --> 47:03.690
and catch a bigger fish.

47:03.690 --> 47:05.191
What? Bait?

47:05.191 --> 47:07.819
From now on, you do exactly what I tell you.

47:07.819 --> 47:09.362
You think I'm crazy?

47:09.362 --> 47:12.398
Just do it when I tell you to.
Why do you talk so much, you punk?

47:13.320 --> 47:15.493
Seriously...

47:15.493 --> 47:17.412
Sit down.

47:17.412 --> 47:18.830
I said sit!

47:18.830 --> 47:20.573
Jeez.

47:23.960 --> 47:27.839
Those two guys who
got caught with you yesterday, remember?

47:27.839 --> 47:31.593
The one with the messed-up face,
that's Bulgae.

47:31.593 --> 47:33.928
Huh? Bulgae? Him?

47:33.928 --> 47:35.347
Then what about the item? Did you find it?

47:35.347 --> 47:36.431
No,

47:36.431 --> 47:39.059
that's what you're going to find out now.

47:39.059 --> 47:42.520
You tail Bulgae and find that item
no matter what.

47:42.520 --> 47:44.522
I'm not crazy.

47:44.522 --> 47:45.774
You think I'm gonna do it?

47:45.774 --> 47:47.725
Be your errand boy?

47:49.027 --> 47:50.728
Oh, yeah?

47:52.322 --> 47:54.857
After seeing this,
you still don't want to do it?

47:58.495 --> 48:00.279
You darn punk!

48:03.958 --> 48:05.293
Should I upload this video

48:05.293 --> 48:08.463
to every gangster group chat out there?

48:08.463 --> 48:10.590
Please, I'm begging you.

48:10.590 --> 48:12.050
Please don't do that.

48:12.050 --> 48:14.344
- So you'll do as I say?
- Yeah.

48:14.344 --> 48:16.471
Then I'll pave the way

48:16.471 --> 48:19.224
for your revenge with a red carpet.

48:19.224 --> 48:22.551
I've got scores to settle with them too.

48:28.358 --> 48:31.694
I'll be the only one calling you,
so pick up within ten seconds.

48:31.694 --> 48:34.155
Even one second late,

48:34.155 --> 48:35.856
you know what happens, huh?

48:47.252 --> 48:49.745
Nam Il, are you done packing?

48:50.505 --> 48:51.798
What, are we fleeing in the dead of night?

48:51.798 --> 48:53.800
Why are we packing all of a sudden?

48:53.800 --> 48:56.010
You wanna get dragged off
and beaten half to death again?

48:56.010 --> 48:57.720
Stop talking and keep packing.

48:57.720 --> 48:58.930
They said three days,

48:58.930 --> 49:00.974
but who knows
when they'll come barging in again.

49:00.974 --> 49:02.058
Where are we even going?

49:02.058 --> 49:04.844
You've got no money and no friends, Uncle.

49:08.606 --> 49:10.307
Come on!

49:11.359 --> 49:13.862
You just don't know it.
Plenty of places want me.

49:13.862 --> 49:16.328
Then you go where you're called, Uncle.

49:16.328 --> 49:18.533
- I'll stay at my friend's place.
- You lost the house

49:18.533 --> 49:20.827
chasing after those "friends,"
and now you're going back to them again?

49:20.827 --> 49:22.287
Quit talking nonsense and pack up!

49:22.287 --> 49:25.322
We need to leave before it's too late.

49:29.252 --> 49:30.962
Uncle.

49:30.962 --> 49:32.788
Where are we going?

49:43.683 --> 49:45.384
Here.

49:51.609 --> 49:55.311
Put the luggage over there. That way,
people won't notice us coming and going.

49:57.780 --> 50:01.326
This tiny room attached to your company
cafeteria is the only place we've got?

50:01.326 --> 50:02.827
What?

50:02.827 --> 50:04.996
It's cozy and nice.

50:04.996 --> 50:08.712
If you take a nap here,
you'll sleep like a baby.

50:12.008 --> 50:14.839
What are we, parasites?

50:14.839 --> 50:17.288
- We should just get a motel!
- Shh!

50:18.259 --> 50:20.178
Quit whining.

50:20.178 --> 50:24.048
We need to save every penny
so that we can get the house back, right?

50:26.392 --> 50:29.521
What if we get caught?
Won't you get fired from the company?

50:29.521 --> 50:33.566
What difference does it make
if I come tomorrow or sleep here tonight?

50:33.566 --> 50:36.602
Stop complaining and get in already!

50:38.568 --> 50:40.136
Shh!

51:11.521 --> 51:13.640
I prepped all the ingredients for today.

51:13.640 --> 51:16.651
- Then I'll leave the lunch service to you.
- W-What...

51:16.651 --> 51:17.694
Leave what to me?

51:17.694 --> 51:20.446
First, there are two targets
we need to keep tabs on.

51:20.446 --> 51:23.491
First, there's Yoo In Goo,
now Han Kyung Wook's right-hand man.

51:23.491 --> 51:27.412
He currently leads the In Goo faction
and serves as president of Heaven Capital.

51:27.412 --> 51:29.372
There's got to be a reason

51:29.372 --> 51:31.958
he's running a loan shark business
here on Yeongseondo Island.

51:31.958 --> 51:35.211
I'll dig into his background
and figure out his motives.

51:35.211 --> 51:36.546
Next is Bulgae.

51:36.546 --> 51:38.339
Former North Korean special agent.

51:38.339 --> 51:39.966
Current name, Bong Jae Soon.

51:39.966 --> 51:42.760
According to our investigation,
he's lived on Yeongseondo Island

51:42.760 --> 51:45.263
with Heo Bong Pil and his grandson
Heo Nam Il for ten years.

51:45.263 --> 51:46.598
Mr. Heo Bong Pil is now dead.

51:46.598 --> 51:49.392
Now, he lives alone with a high schooler
named Heo Nam Il.

51:49.392 --> 51:50.852
Currently,

51:50.852 --> 51:54.814
he works as a supervisor at Yeongseon Steel,
a rebar processing plant.

51:54.814 --> 51:56.107
Now this guy.

51:56.107 --> 51:58.026
Ma Gong Bok, you're good at
digging into people's backgrounds,

51:58.026 --> 51:59.852
so you take him.

52:00.570 --> 52:01.696
Jeez.

52:01.696 --> 52:04.574
He's been telling people
around him that he has amnesia,

52:04.574 --> 52:07.118
but there's a very high chance
he's faking it.

52:07.118 --> 52:09.245
Figure out exactly what he's after.

52:09.245 --> 52:12.290
Our goal is to find the item.

52:12.290 --> 52:14.250
Please just give me ten days,

52:14.250 --> 52:16.744
and I'll pay it back, sir!

52:17.879 --> 52:19.756
Sir!

52:19.756 --> 52:21.549
No, please don't!

52:21.549 --> 52:23.917
Oh no, oh no...

52:25.929 --> 52:26.929
If you need anything,

52:26.929 --> 52:29.256
- just call me right away.
- Take care.

52:33.061 --> 52:34.729
- Gong Bok!
- Yes, you're here?

52:34.729 --> 52:37.940
- I checked the numbers, and yesterday...
- Yes, thank you.

52:37.940 --> 52:40.392
W-We're short 300 won!

52:48.743 --> 52:51.120
- We'll take them out, boss.
- Please!

52:51.120 --> 52:52.664
Honey!

52:52.664 --> 52:55.240
Let's do it in one go! Okay?

52:56.456 --> 52:59.495
Just press here. Enough, let go.

53:00.296 --> 53:02.674
Relax, relax.

53:02.674 --> 53:05.084
That's it.

53:10.807 --> 53:12.475
Ah, these punks

53:12.475 --> 53:15.019
are threatening people who have
gambling debts and borrowed from loan sharks,

53:15.019 --> 53:18.731
grabbing up every bit of land
on Yeongseondo Island.

53:18.731 --> 53:19.857
Hey, gangster,

53:19.857 --> 53:21.109
there's gotta be a reason

53:21.109 --> 53:23.752
you guys are squeezing people
like this, right?

53:23.752 --> 53:26.030
- Tell me.
- Ah, seriously...

53:26.030 --> 53:28.282
Don't lump us in with trash like Yoo In Goo.

53:28.282 --> 53:29.659
Our main business was entertainment.

53:29.659 --> 53:31.619
We never touched dirty business like this.

53:31.619 --> 53:34.414
Different business, same kind of thugs.
You should know something.

53:34.414 --> 53:36.416
- So what is it?
- Can't you tell just by looking?

53:36.416 --> 53:39.293
It's a typical land grab
in redevelopment areas.

53:39.293 --> 53:41.629
They buy up land at dirt-cheap prices,

53:41.629 --> 53:43.297
wait for redevelopment approval,

53:43.297 --> 53:45.842
and then cash out and disappear.
Classic holdout scheme.

53:45.842 --> 53:47.593
So what these punks are doing

53:47.593 --> 53:49.512
is just a simple redevelopment scheme?

53:49.512 --> 53:51.305
Still,

53:51.305 --> 53:53.474
something smells fishy.

53:53.474 --> 53:55.184
If it were Gangnam land in Seoul, maybe.

53:55.184 --> 53:57.729
But the land here isn't worth much.
Why bother going through the hassle?

53:57.729 --> 53:59.897
It doesn't look like
there's much to gain from it.

53:59.897 --> 54:01.733
Han Kyung Wook's main campaign promise is

54:01.733 --> 54:04.193
large-scale Yeongseondo Island
development, right?

54:04.193 --> 54:07.229
They're just dipping their toes
into the development business.

54:07.905 --> 54:10.315
Maybe you're barking up the wrong tree.

54:11.409 --> 54:14.328
Are you saying that because you don't know
what kind of man Han Kyung Wook is?

54:14.328 --> 54:17.749
You really think he's doing this
just to develop Yeongseondo Island?

54:17.749 --> 54:19.450
I don't know.

54:21.002 --> 54:23.787
Well, anyway,

54:35.683 --> 54:37.185
What's this?

54:37.185 --> 54:39.812
Darn it, who told you
to take pictures like this?

54:39.812 --> 54:42.273
What's this? Why'd you take pictures
of him eating ramyeon?

54:42.273 --> 54:43.656
Why did you take these pictures?

54:43.656 --> 54:46.986
He's stuck in the company 24/7,
so what am I supposed to do about it?

54:46.986 --> 54:48.362
After losing his house to Yoo In Goo,

54:48.362 --> 54:50.531
he practically lives hidden
inside the company now.

54:50.531 --> 54:52.909
He never comes outside!

54:52.909 --> 54:54.577
You...

54:54.577 --> 54:56.287
Fine, look at this.

54:56.287 --> 54:59.156
I've got this video ready to upload...

55:01.709 --> 55:03.544
I did everything you asked. This isn't fair!

55:03.544 --> 55:06.422
That only counts
if you actually investigated properly.

55:06.422 --> 55:08.680
If you come back empty-handed again,

55:08.680 --> 55:10.542
this video's going straight
onto NewTube, got it?

55:12.929 --> 55:14.806
Do we really have to do this here?

55:14.806 --> 55:18.258
I'm basically a semi-pro
at washing people. Get over here.

55:25.288 --> 55:26.728
Come on!

55:27.860 --> 55:29.362
This isn't right, this isn't right.

55:29.362 --> 55:30.530
Uncle! You go wash up first.

55:30.530 --> 55:32.198
You stink, stink, stink!

55:32.198 --> 55:34.450
Your body reeks, okay?

55:34.450 --> 55:36.744
I can't sleep because you smell like crap.

55:36.744 --> 55:37.829
What smell?

55:37.829 --> 55:40.614
I washed up a week ago!

55:42.959 --> 55:44.660
Bend down.

55:56.639 --> 55:59.424
What the heck are you doing in here?

56:02.813 --> 56:03.813
So,

56:03.813 --> 56:06.107
because of your nephew's gambling debts,

56:06.107 --> 56:08.442
Heaven Capital took your house

56:08.442 --> 56:10.194
and now you're

56:10.194 --> 56:13.063
secretly living at the company?

56:14.407 --> 56:16.742
Seriously, what are you thinking?

56:16.742 --> 56:20.413
Are you trying to invent
some creative new way to get fired?

56:20.413 --> 56:21.989
Ms. Lee...

56:23.332 --> 56:25.459
Just let this slide, please.

56:25.459 --> 56:27.837
You think I'd do this if I had a choice?

56:27.837 --> 56:29.630
Just for a little while.

56:29.630 --> 56:31.757
Only until I can save enough
to get the house back.

56:31.757 --> 56:33.959
And what if this blows back on me?

56:39.891 --> 56:42.759
If you get caught,
I don't know anything about this.

56:44.145 --> 56:45.897
Ms. Lee,

56:45.897 --> 56:47.398
I'll fix this somehow.

56:47.398 --> 56:48.691
I'll figure something out.

56:48.691 --> 56:50.726
Thank you, Ms. Lee, really.

57:00.745 --> 57:02.496
The amount is correct, right?

57:02.496 --> 57:04.615
Yeah, barely managed to balance it.

57:05.666 --> 57:07.752
But, boss,

57:07.752 --> 57:10.129
are you sure this is okay?

57:10.129 --> 57:12.006
I mean, all the money from Capital

57:12.006 --> 57:14.759
and even the In Goo faction is in this safe.

57:14.759 --> 57:15.927
If this goes sideways,

57:15.927 --> 57:18.054
we won't even have money left
to loan out, boss.

57:18.054 --> 57:19.096
You punk,

57:19.096 --> 57:21.557
you've got the guts of a bean.

57:21.557 --> 57:23.893
You don't know 'high risk, high return'?

57:23.893 --> 57:27.730
If this deal goes through,
we'll make ten times back or even more.

57:27.730 --> 57:32.485
Watch closely and learn how
I build the In Goo faction.

57:32.485 --> 57:33.527
You're here, boss.

57:33.527 --> 57:35.228
Oh.

57:35.863 --> 57:37.657
You're here, boss.

57:37.657 --> 57:38.783
What about the Chinese guys?

57:38.783 --> 57:40.692
They're waiting inside.

58:01.597 --> 58:03.683
As expected, Mr. Yoo.

58:03.683 --> 58:06.093
Love how decisively you handle things.

58:07.770 --> 58:09.397
Those mainland guys were really picky,

58:09.397 --> 58:11.807
so setting up the deal was rough.

58:13.860 --> 58:16.362
- What about the rest of the shipment?
- The shipment's huge,

58:16.362 --> 58:18.197
so we're working our tails off
to produce it now.

58:18.197 --> 58:20.825
We'll bring the whole batch next deal day.

58:20.825 --> 58:23.369
With this quality,
it'd make a splash in Gangnam.

58:23.369 --> 58:24.829
Gangnam's nothing.

58:24.829 --> 58:28.374
From here on out, it's all about
the money for the In Goo faction.

58:28.374 --> 58:30.793
Good work, Mr. Choi.

58:30.793 --> 58:34.255
Make sure the mainland guys get off
to a good start, and keep them in line.

58:34.255 --> 58:36.215
Come on, this isn't some corner shop.

58:36.215 --> 58:37.842
It's the top drug production line
on the mainland.

58:37.842 --> 58:40.261
I don't even need to keep them in line.
They're sharp with deals.

58:40.261 --> 58:43.055
Mr. Yoo, you just focus on the deal date.

58:43.055 --> 58:45.266
You're worrying for nothing.

58:45.266 --> 58:48.227
Still, something's off.
I smell something fishy.

58:48.227 --> 58:49.895
I mean, think about it logically.

58:49.895 --> 58:52.898
What they're doing at Capital
is suspicious enough already,

58:52.898 --> 58:55.183
and now they're running a jerky factory?

58:55.943 --> 58:58.863
What on earth are they actually up to?

58:58.863 --> 59:01.449
Isn't that jerky factory just a front?

59:01.449 --> 59:02.908
For kidnapping people and beating them up?

59:02.908 --> 59:06.454
That's what I thought too,
but they're actually producing real jerky.

59:06.454 --> 59:08.330
You said Yoo In Goo
took over the Hwasan faction

59:08.330 --> 59:10.791
and teamed up with Han Kyung Wook, right?

59:10.791 --> 59:11.876
Then obviously,

59:11.876 --> 59:14.661
he must be operating
under Han Kyung Wook's orders.

59:15.546 --> 59:19.258
So what the on earth are they
doing on Yeongseondo Island?

59:19.258 --> 59:21.427
What about that other Hwasan guy?

59:21.427 --> 59:23.554
That Ma Gong Bok or whatever, is he any good?

59:23.554 --> 59:25.473
I'm only using him because I'm short-staffed.

59:25.473 --> 59:28.759
I mean, how can I trust a guy
who was just some small-time gangster?

59:30.227 --> 59:32.980
Whether it's Bulgae or Yoo In Goo,

59:32.980 --> 59:34.190
no matter what,

59:34.190 --> 59:35.900
I need to settle this.

59:35.900 --> 59:37.476
Settle it?

59:39.278 --> 59:41.563
What are you thinking right now?

59:43.115 --> 59:44.742
I have a bad feeling.

59:44.742 --> 59:47.328
Feels like it's time to make a move.

59:47.328 --> 59:48.662
No, Ho Myung! Don't!

59:48.662 --> 59:50.414
The situation's still unclear.

59:50.414 --> 59:52.833
Let's move when things are clearer.

59:52.833 --> 59:55.294
No, that's pointless.

59:55.294 --> 59:56.921
Then what are you gonna do?

59:56.921 --> 59:58.881
Looks like

59:58.881 --> 01:00:00.591
I need to have a little meeting

01:00:00.591 --> 01:00:02.176
with Yoo In Goo.

01:00:02.176 --> 01:00:03.385
A meeting?

01:00:03.385 --> 01:00:05.012
Alone?

01:00:05.012 --> 01:00:07.297
Since when did I ever partner with anyone?

01:00:09.892 --> 01:00:12.728
Wow, look how white this powder is.

01:00:12.728 --> 01:00:16.065
Wow, this is definitely top-grade, boss.

01:00:16.065 --> 01:00:17.316
Hey,

01:00:17.316 --> 01:00:20.778
if we keep getting this quality stuff
on the next deal,

01:00:20.778 --> 01:00:23.155
it'll sell out instantly

01:00:23.155 --> 01:00:25.324
and the money will pour in like crazy.

01:00:25.324 --> 01:00:26.408
Then

01:00:26.408 --> 01:00:31.455
we're done scrambling around
cleaning up messes for Mr. Han.

01:00:31.455 --> 01:00:33.165
You're right, boss.

01:00:33.165 --> 01:00:34.458
- Kang Sik.
- Yes?

01:00:34.458 --> 01:00:37.702
We had a good deal today,
so let's hit a nice place for a change.

01:00:41.674 --> 01:00:44.176
I'm going to the bathroom.
Everyone stay on standby.

01:00:44.176 --> 01:00:46.211
Got it. Go ahead, boss.

01:00:51.642 --> 01:00:54.312
- Go ahead, boss.
- Yeah.

01:00:54.312 --> 01:00:57.288
Come on, guys.

01:01:19.420 --> 01:01:22.173
Your stream doesn't sound very healthy.

01:01:22.173 --> 01:01:24.508
I know a good prostate clinic.

01:01:24.508 --> 01:01:25.926
Want me

01:01:25.926 --> 01:01:28.762
to introduce it to you?

01:01:28.762 --> 01:01:30.672
Mr. Yoo In Goo?

01:01:32.224 --> 01:01:34.259
What's up with you punk...

01:01:51.035 --> 01:01:52.828
Jeez, now I've got pee all over me.

01:01:52.828 --> 01:01:54.529
You're dead!

01:02:01.879 --> 01:02:04.006
Who on earth are you? Who sent you?

01:02:04.006 --> 01:02:05.549
Can't you tell?

01:02:05.549 --> 01:02:08.093
I'm the Masked Racer!

01:02:08.093 --> 01:02:10.554
Here to punish scumbags like you!

01:02:10.554 --> 01:02:12.797
The Masked Racer!

01:02:14.475 --> 01:02:17.344
Is this crazy punk out of his mind?

01:02:18.312 --> 01:02:19.396
Listen.

01:02:19.396 --> 01:02:20.564
I've been watching

01:02:20.564 --> 01:02:23.359
all the crap you guys have been
up to the past few days.

01:02:23.359 --> 01:02:26.862
But no matter how much I think about it,
there's something I just don't get.

01:02:26.862 --> 01:02:28.197
So I'm gonna ask you a few questions.

01:02:28.197 --> 01:02:31.912
How do you plan to handle
the aftermath? Darn it!

01:02:39.875 --> 01:02:41.252
Talk.

01:02:41.252 --> 01:02:43.629
Why are you In Goo faction punks

01:02:43.629 --> 01:02:46.215
causing trouble on Yeongseondo Island?

01:02:46.215 --> 01:02:49.928
Why are you threatening people
and taking their homes and land?

01:02:49.928 --> 01:02:51.679
Darn it,

01:02:51.679 --> 01:02:53.922
you've got a lot of questions.

01:03:06.694 --> 01:03:08.195
Believe it or not,

01:03:08.195 --> 01:03:10.572
I'm a humanitarian,

01:03:10.572 --> 01:03:13.984
so I don't really like
beating people up one-sidedly.

01:03:16.787 --> 01:03:17.788
What are you doing?

01:03:17.788 --> 01:03:19.489
Pick that up.

01:03:22.459 --> 01:03:25.418
You're dead, you punk!

01:03:25.418 --> 01:03:27.557
Jeez.

01:03:30.551 --> 01:03:32.553
Well...

01:03:32.553 --> 01:03:36.047
It's been way too long, no?

01:03:36.890 --> 01:03:38.758
Should I go check?

01:03:41.186 --> 01:03:43.605
You punk,

01:03:43.605 --> 01:03:46.558
show some respect.
He's in the bathroom doing his business.

01:04:00.205 --> 01:04:02.082
One last question.

01:04:02.082 --> 01:04:04.126
What is your purpose on Yeongseondo Island?

01:04:04.126 --> 01:04:07.328
I don't know, you punk!

01:04:15.846 --> 01:04:17.222
Do you know

01:04:17.222 --> 01:04:20.726
when humans are most honest?

01:04:20.726 --> 01:04:22.927
When they feel pain.

01:04:23.812 --> 01:04:25.022
I'll talk! I'll talk!

01:04:25.022 --> 01:04:26.190
I'll talk...

01:04:26.190 --> 01:04:27.891
I'm telling you...

01:04:29.026 --> 01:04:30.852
The reason we came

01:04:31.695 --> 01:04:34.856
to Yeongseondo Island is...

01:04:37.224 --> 01:04:39.208
Screw you, you punk!

01:04:52.966 --> 01:04:54.626
That startled me!

01:04:55.848 --> 01:04:57.883
Darn it.

01:05:05.479 --> 01:05:07.347
Pick it up already!

01:05:10.484 --> 01:05:12.444
- Yes, boss!
- Kang Sik!

01:05:12.444 --> 01:05:14.696
- Yes, boss!
- Kang Sik, bathroom! Bathroom, quick!

01:05:14.696 --> 01:05:17.116
- Yes, boss?
- Get to the bathroom now!

01:05:17.116 --> 01:05:20.077
Hey, you little bug! Bathroom!

01:05:20.077 --> 01:05:21.912
Hey! Bathroom, bathroom!

01:05:21.912 --> 01:05:24.039
Hurry up to the bathroom, you punks!

01:05:24.039 --> 01:05:26.407
Yes, boss! Yes!

01:05:34.174 --> 01:05:35.426
I know who you are.

01:05:35.426 --> 01:05:37.678
You're the guy who lost land to me, right?

01:05:37.678 --> 01:05:40.222
The martial arts master, huh?

01:05:40.222 --> 01:05:41.765
I'm the one asking the questions.

01:05:41.765 --> 01:05:44.425
What's your purpose?

01:05:50.274 --> 01:05:52.151
You martial arts master punk!

01:05:52.151 --> 01:05:54.477
You think you'll get out of this unscathed?

01:05:57.239 --> 01:05:58.982
Boss!

01:06:01.118 --> 01:06:02.119
Boss!

01:06:02.119 --> 01:06:03.820
We... Huh?

01:06:06.290 --> 01:06:08.083
What's that?

01:06:08.083 --> 01:06:09.909
Is he the main character or something?

01:06:10.586 --> 01:06:14.038
Hey, you masked punk! You're dead now!

01:06:40.648 --> 01:06:42.760
They say one guy broke In Goo's arm?

01:06:42.760 --> 01:06:44.552
He doesn't seem like an ordinary guy.

01:06:45.352 --> 01:06:46.440
Go get that masked punk.

01:06:46.440 --> 01:06:48.125
Bring him here!

01:06:48.125 --> 01:06:49.384
Let's move!

01:06:49.384 --> 01:06:52.040
The thugs are coming to catch you!

01:06:52.040 --> 01:06:53.444
Hurry up and grab him!

01:06:53.444 --> 01:06:55.720
- Super rich?
- Let's recruit a gatekeeper.

01:06:55.720 --> 01:06:57.800
- Yeah, I'll do it no matter what.
- What do I have to do?

01:06:57.800 --> 01:06:59.784
[D-Day]
The spy incident on the ferry 10 years ago.

01:06:59.784 --> 01:07:02.600
- You know who this person is, right?
- A prosecutor came. A prosecutor.

01:07:02.600 --> 01:07:04.776
- Let's bury him.
- Contact me.

01:07:04.776 --> 01:07:08.040
- Time to wrap things up.
- I was on that ferry.

01:07:08.040 --> 01:07:09.992
Keep this up and you're really going to die.

01:07:09.992 --> 01:07:11.688
Do you have to go in?

01:07:11.688 --> 01:07:14.178
If it's for family,
there's nothing I wouldn't do.
